2] From any host (but squid or openvpn). On squid we do a tcpdump which show what http(s) request reach the squid host on port 443. The stunnel redirect to squid on port 3128 which then decrypted the TLS : the protected header is visible in plain text.
Stunnel will decrypt first TLS layer (then see "dummy-ops.dev, the authentication in plain text, .." but not the header).

$ curl -v -x https://squid.vagrant-dummy-ops.lab --proxy-user 'squid:chocol@tepie94' --proxy-basic -H 'X-Demo-Secret: TLS_BUMP_PROOF_123456' https://dummy-ops.dev/ -o /dev/null

root@squid:~# tcpdump -i eth1 -nn -A 'host 192.168.1.208 and tcp and port 443'
